  "text": "\r\n\t\t Elections | Atkinson, NH \r\n Skip to Main Content \r\nCreate a Website Account   - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.    \r\nWebsite Sign In \r\n     About   \t\t\t \n     Departments   \t\t\t \n     Boards & Committees   \t\t\t \n     Find It Fast   \t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t Search \n\t\t\t 9.8.2026 State Primary Election Information & Sample Ballots \r\n\t\t\t Absentee Ballot Information - Town & State/Federal \r\n\t\t\t NH Election State Laws \r\n\t\t\t NH Election Information \r\n\t\t\t Town Elections \r\n\t\t\t Citizen's Petition Guidelines (PDF) \r\n\t\t\t Citizen's Petition Warrant Article \r\n\t\t\t Forms & Documents \r\n\t\t\t Historical Election Results \r\n\t\t\t Town Clerk's Office \r\nHome \nDepartments \nElections \r\nElections\t\t \r\nNews Flash \r\n\t NH State Election - Tues., 11/3/26 - Learn More  \r\nAbsentee ballots are available at the Clerk's office until 5pm on Monday, 11/2/2026.  The Town Clerk's Office will close at 5pm (not 6:30pm) on Tuesday, 11/3/26.\t\t\t\t Read on... \r\n\t\t View All News \r\n/CivicAlerts.aspx \r\nElections / Voter Information \nElections & Voter Registrations \nIn order to participate in local or state elections and meetings, you must be registered to vote. You may register to vote at the Town Clerk's office more than 6 to 13 days prior to an election, depending on when the supervisors of the checklist meet to finalize the voter checklist, or at the polls on an election (not meeting) day. You must be 18 years of age or older on the day of the next election, a U.S. citizen, and domiciled in Atkinson. You must present proof of age, identification, domicile, and citizenship. You may present a birth certificate, passport, or naturalization papers as proof of citizenship.  \nSee the Secretary of State's website for additional  Voter Registration Information . \nTo change party affiliation, voters must bring their government-issued photo ID into the Town Clerk's office and complete a new Voter Registration Form indicating their party change. This may be done any time that the Town Clerk is open except for the period of time between the first day of a filing period for a primary election and the election itself. \nYou may also attend a Supervisors of the Checklist meeting to register to vote or make changes to your voter registration address, party, name, etc...  \r\nAdditional Election / Voter Information \nModerator's Notice about signs and electioneering at the polling place \nGuide to registering to vote in NH \nElection Warrant \nNH Primary Information \nElectioneering Flyer \nElection Results \r\nMore about the Supervisors of the Checklist \nSupervisors of the Checklist have final authority over the addition, removal, and updating of voters in Atkinson.  Once approved, all registered voters will appear on the public voter list available at the Kimball Library and Town Clerk office.  The Supervisors are required to meet at least every 90 days or more often based on the election schedule each year.  \nThe Atkinson Supervisors of the Checklist will be meeting on  Tuesday , October 27, 2026, from 6pm - 6:30pm, at the Atkinson Town Hall , to update the voter checklist, accept party affiliation changes, accept new voter registrations, and address/name changes. \nYou may register to vote, update your name and/or address, and/or party affiliation changes in-person at the Town Clerk's Office during business hours or in-person or at a Supervisor of the Checklist meeting.  If newly registering to vote in NH, we will ask you to bring a U.S. Passport or Certified Original Birth Certificate if available.  \nState of New Hampshire voter information look-up . \nFor more information about voting in NH or other state election information, visit the  NH Secretary of State website . \r\nContact Us \r\n\t\t\t\t\tJulianna  Hale\r\nTown Clerk/Tax Collector \r\nPhone:  603-362-4920 \r\nElections \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Physical Address \r\n View Map \t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Town Hall \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 19 Academy Avenue \n\t\t\t\t\t Atkinson ,  NH   03811 \r\nTown Hall 19 Academy Avenue Atkinson NH 03811 \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t Directions \r\nPhone:  603-362-4920 \r\nFax: 603-362-5305 \r\nHours \nMonday \n8:30 am to 5 pm \nTuesday \n8:30 am to 6:30 pm \nWednesday & Thursday \n8:30 am to 5 pm \nFridays \n8 am to 12 pm \r\nDirectory \r\nFAQs \r\n             How do I register to vote or update my voting information? \r\n         View All FAQs \r\n/FAQ.aspx \r\n\t\t\t Online Payments \r\n\t\t\t Applications & \nLicenses \r\n\t\t\t Minutes, Agendas & Public Notices \r\n\t\t\t Department Hours \r\n\t\t\t Property Taxes \r\n\t\t\t Trash & Recycling \r\nTown of Atkinson \r\n19 Academy Avenue \r\nAtkinson, NH 03811 \r\nPhone:  603-362-5266 \r\n         Job Opportunities \n         Volunteer Opportunities \n         Subscribe \n         Elections \n         Photos \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\n         Home \n         Contact Us \n         Accessibility \n         Site Map \n         Copyright Notices \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\n   Government Websites by  CivicPlus® \nLoading \r\n\t\t\t\tLoading\r\n\t\t\t Do Not Show Again \r\n\t\t\t Close \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Left \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Right \r\n[] \r\n                     Slideshow Left Arrow \r\n                     Slideshow Right Arrow \r\n ",
